message: "If you use this cookbook, please cite it as below."
authors:
  - family-names: Buchanan
    given-names: Glen
    website: https://github.com/glenbuchanan
  - name: "CESM2 LENS ML Readiness Cookbook contributors"
    website: "https://github.com/glenbuchanan/cesm2-lens-ml-readiness-cookbook/graphs/contributors"
title: "CESM2 LENS ML Readiness Cookbook"
abstract: "A supervised classification on NSF NCAR's CESM2 Large Ensemble (the AWS Open Data copy): does the autumn ENSO state predict a wet Front Range winter? The notebook follows NSF Unidata's Supervised Machine Learning Readiness spine — framing, metadata document, explore, split, train, validate, refine, test, justify — with one change made on purpose: the split is by ensemble member, because the question is about members the model has never seen and because the forced-response curve and the wet threshold are fit on training members only, inside each validation fold. The notebook measures, rather than assumes, what a member-blind split or a transform fit before the split does to the score. A handbook and rubric score eleven recorded exercises, including saying plainly when no model beats the base rate. On the model's own winters no model is shown to beat the base rate, and the notebook treats that as the result. Drafted with AI assistance (Anthropic's Claude) from cited sources, under the author's direction."
